From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abue Ammar <14371506+abue-ammar@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 06:48:37 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] Add custom request headers to AI API connections (#1680)

The connection editor gets a Request Headers section of name/value rows.
The headers go to model discovery and every chat request after the
route's own, so a custom name replaces a default in any case. With
headers set the API key is optional, and an empty key now sends no
credential header instead of an empty one.

Values live in one Keychain item per connection under a new
ai-request-headers scope; nothing is added to AIConnection, so settings
backups and settings.json are untouched. Removing a connection deletes
its headers with its key. Header values are redacted from provider
errors like the key.

KeychainSecretStore gains values(for:)/setValues(_:for:) for a JSON
dictionary item, and the installed-AI environment store now uses them
instead of its own copy of that code.
